WEBVTT

00:03.390 --> 00:05.050
Well, it's official.

00:05.740 --> 00:07.140
Fall is here.

00:09.230 --> 00:10.680
Right?

00:12.240 --> 00:13.790
Right?

00:15.560 --> 00:16.890
Right?!

00:17.990 --> 00:18.830
Yeah.

00:19.170 --> 00:20.240
Yeah.

00:20.240 --> 00:23.120
Just when we've overcome the pool crisis...

00:23.120 --> 00:25.880
We now face a new challenge, Miyamura-kun.

00:25.880 --> 00:28.100
We do, President.

00:28.100 --> 00:30.000
<i>It's like they're holding a wake.</i>

00:30.700 --> 00:33.260
I'm here at last!

00:33.580 --> 00:37.540
And I've brought the team 
assignments for sports day!

00:38.290 --> 00:39.260
Wait, huh?

00:39.260 --> 00:43.270
<b>Ba-dump Ba-dump</b>

00:39.260 --> 00:43.270
<b>Ba-dump</b>

00:40.130 --> 00:41.910
This <i>is</i> where I turn 'em in, right?

00:41.910 --> 00:43.270
Yes...

00:45.770 --> 00:47.830
As each class brings in their forms,

00:47.830 --> 00:50.620
I feel sports day creeping closer and closer.

00:50.620 --> 00:54.150
That's not just a feeling. 
It really is getting closer.

00:54.150 --> 00:56.280
<b>AAAAAAAAAAGH</b>

00:56.280 --> 00:59.200
<b>AAAAAAAAAAGH</b>

01:01.160 --> 01:02.400
A rain dance!

01:02.700 --> 01:04.040
Rain dance! Rain dance!

01:04.440 --> 01:06.540
Rain dance! Rain dance!

01:06.540 --> 01:09.290
Excuse me! Here are our team assignments...

01:06.540 --> 01:11.960
Rain dance! Rain dance!

01:09.640 --> 01:10.720
What's going on?!

02:42.510 --> 02:48.020
<b>Cooking Class</b>

02:44.840 --> 02:48.020
Does each class decide team 
assignments by drawing lots?

02:48.020 --> 02:52.500
<b>East\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWest</b>

02:48.020 --> 02:52.500
Boys & Girls




(Half)

02:48.020 --> 02:52.500
Boys & Girls




(Half)

02:48.020 --> 02:55.020
<b>Katagiri High Sports Day Teams Splitting</b>

02:48.600 --> 02:51.730
To keep the number of boys and 
girls balanced on each team,

02:50.830 --> 02:55.020
<b>East\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWest</b>

02:50.830 --> 02:55.020
Boys & Girls




(Half)

02:50.830 --> 02:55.020
Boys & Girls




(Half)

02:51.730 --> 02:55.020
each class first divides into boys 
and girls, then assigns teams.

02:55.020 --> 02:58.650
I expect most of them only draw 
for which team they'll be on.

02:58.650 --> 03:03.050
It must feel pretty weird to be 
going up against your own classmates.

03:03.050 --> 03:06.540
Yeah, I'm glad we're on 
the same team, Ishikawa-kun.

03:06.950 --> 03:08.920
By the way, what team are you on, Sengoku?

03:09.490 --> 03:10.410
East.

03:10.410 --> 03:14.670
<b>West</b>

03:11.800 --> 03:13.040
Why are you cheering?

03:13.040 --> 03:14.670
Don't act so relieved!

03:15.080 --> 03:16.170
Sengoku.

03:16.960 --> 03:18.530
I'm counting on you.

03:18.530 --> 03:19.840
<i>Seriously?</i>

03:20.460 --> 03:21.670
Wait.

03:21.670 --> 03:24.800
So you and Miyamura-kun split up?

03:25.110 --> 03:27.500
We did <i>not</i> split up. I oughta deck you.

03:27.500 --> 03:29.310
I meant for sports day.

03:29.770 --> 03:32.650
I'm not going to lose to Toru and Miyamura.

03:32.650 --> 03:34.500
Okay. Good luck to you.

03:34.500 --> 03:36.260
Good luck to <i>us</i>.

03:36.690 --> 03:39.290
Yuki and Iura are on our team, too.

03:36.690 --> 03:41.950
<b>Way too excited for sports day</b>

03:39.610 --> 03:41.950
<i>Seriously?</i>

03:42.380 --> 03:47.110
That means I won't be able to 
stay out of sight and do nothing...

03:47.110 --> 03:50.450
You just casually made a pretty 
loaded confession, President.

03:50.860 --> 03:53.860
<i>I thought he was absent, 
but he was staying out of sight?</i>

03:54.310 --> 03:57.960
Say, the girls are gonna do
a cheer routine this year, right?

03:58.650 --> 04:00.970
Will you be participating, Sakura?

04:01.810 --> 04:02.870
I will.

04:03.800 --> 04:05.720
It's mandatory.

04:06.040 --> 04:09.770
For everyone. Even if they
have no sense of rhythm.

04:10.720 --> 04:13.480
Your voice sounds awfully low today...

04:13.480 --> 04:15.890
We'll need to make pom-poms.

04:15.890 --> 04:17.040
Indeed.

04:17.040 --> 04:19.840
I hope the steps aren't too difficult.

04:19.840 --> 04:21.950
Are you east or west, Kono-san?

04:21.950 --> 04:23.530
I'm on the west team.

04:23.530 --> 04:24.930
So is Remi.

04:24.930 --> 04:26.410
I guess that makes us rivals.

04:26.410 --> 04:28.890
Toru and Miyamura are west, too.

04:30.170 --> 04:32.620
<i>I'm on the same team as Ishikawa-kun...</i>

04:34.120 --> 04:35.960
<b>Last year's nightmare</b>

04:36.210 --> 04:40.240
<i>And he's going to see me out 
there flailing like an idiot!</i>

04:40.880 --> 04:43.020
Rain dance! Do a rain dance!

04:43.020 --> 04:45.130
Okay, Sakura, we'll do one together!

04:46.120 --> 04:48.030
Rain! Rain!

04:48.030 --> 04:50.140
<i>Is the student council okay?</i>

04:48.030 --> 04:50.760
Rain! Rain!

04:52.770 --> 04:57.990
Honestly, Sengoku's always been clumsy...

04:58.690 --> 05:01.780
but as the council president, 
he needs to get it together.

05:01.780 --> 05:05.640
I guess he's never been much of an athlete.

05:05.640 --> 05:08.410
Pretty much. I remember him 
tripping and crying a lot.

05:08.450 --> 05:12.910
<b>Came home covered in dirt
after running amok at sports day</b>

05:09.510 --> 05:12.240
He could learn a thing or two from Sota.

05:12.910 --> 05:14.710
Huh? Oh...

05:15.110 --> 05:16.520
Y'know...

05:18.050 --> 05:21.780
I don't have any fond memories 
of sports days either.

05:25.500 --> 05:29.200
You're a good runner, 
so enter the 100-meter dash.

05:29.200 --> 05:30.140
But...

05:30.140 --> 05:31.560
No buts!

05:32.130 --> 05:34.060
Give us everything you've got!

05:35.750 --> 05:37.930
I'll be doing the same.

05:37.930 --> 05:40.440
Absolutely no slacking. Or else!

05:42.530 --> 05:47.700
I'm not really an athlete myself, 
but I think it'll be more fun than last year.

05:48.320 --> 05:49.350
Call it a hunch.

05:50.930 --> 05:53.680
So I should do my best 
in the 100-meter dash?

05:53.680 --> 05:54.970
Your absolute best.

05:54.970 --> 05:57.500
And I should cheer a lot?

05:57.500 --> 05:59.160
As much as you can.

05:59.160 --> 06:01.710
Will you cheer for me?

06:01.710 --> 06:03.920
Of course I will!

06:03.920 --> 06:06.020
We're on different teams, though.

06:06.460 --> 06:07.230
I...

06:07.230 --> 06:09.230
I know that.

06:10.550 --> 06:12.350
But I'll still be watching.

06:14.300 --> 06:15.300
Okay.

06:15.720 --> 06:17.550
<i>How strange.</i>

06:17.550 --> 06:20.730
<i>I used to wish it would
be over as soon as possible,</i>

06:21.530 --> 06:24.060
<i>but now I'm actually looking forward to it.</i>

06:25.200 --> 06:28.480
<i>Yo, Miyamura! Can I swing by 
tomorrow evening?</i>

06:28.480 --> 06:31.670
No, I'm getting ready for sports day.

06:33.180 --> 06:36.260
<i>We did ours in June.</i>

06:36.260 --> 06:38.750
<i>What are you entering? Or are you skipping?</i>

06:39.270 --> 06:43.180
<i>I haven't decided, 
but I might do the 100-meter dash.</i>

06:44.230 --> 06:45.500
Whoa.

06:45.950 --> 06:47.510
<i>You sound surprisingly motivated.</i>

06:48.530 --> 06:51.600
Yeah. I surprisingly am.

06:53.080 --> 06:54.260
Nice.

06:54.900 --> 06:57.230
<i>I might just come watch!</i>

06:57.230 --> 06:58.670
Don't, jerk.

07:00.720 --> 07:02.520
<i>I think the days ahead</i>

07:03.960 --> 07:06.370
<i>will be a little more lively than usual.</i>

07:08.140 --> 07:11.160
That's enough for today. Good work!

07:13.820 --> 07:15.390
This is hard.

07:16.660 --> 07:19.200
<i>I'm the only one having 
trouble with the moves.</i>

07:19.600 --> 07:22.240
<i>At this rate, I'll make 
a fool of myself this year, too.</i>

07:22.960 --> 07:24.290
<i>And this year...</i>

07:24.940 --> 07:28.300
<i>And this year, Ishikawa-kun 
might be watching.</i>

07:30.140 --> 07:31.460
Kono-san?

07:32.510 --> 07:34.190
Yoshikawa-san?

07:34.190 --> 07:35.550
What's the matter?

07:35.880 --> 07:37.590
A-Are you not feeling well?

07:37.590 --> 07:39.600
No, that's not it!

07:39.600 --> 07:41.830
So it's something else? Are you okay?

07:42.220 --> 07:44.840
We were just practicing our cheer routine.

07:44.840 --> 07:47.140
Wait, was there cheer practice today?

07:47.140 --> 07:50.060
Oh, I'm on the west team.

07:50.060 --> 07:52.450
Gotcha. I'm east.

07:52.850 --> 07:57.130
I'm not athletic,
and I have no sense of rhythm...

07:57.130 --> 07:59.330
so it's really getting the better of me.

08:01.700 --> 08:03.840
I'm sorry! It's nothing.

08:03.840 --> 08:06.710
I'll practice a little more.

08:07.220 --> 08:09.090
Right. Left.

08:09.090 --> 08:10.970
Left. Right.

08:10.970 --> 08:13.470
W-Wait, was it left? Um...

08:14.570 --> 08:16.770
Is that the part both teams do?

08:16.770 --> 08:17.470
Huh?

08:17.470 --> 08:18.560
Right!

08:20.970 --> 08:23.870
When your right hand goes up,
put your left to your chest.

08:23.870 --> 08:25.030
Do it with me now.

08:25.030 --> 08:26.510
O-Okay.

08:27.200 --> 08:29.210
Hit the other side twice.

08:29.660 --> 08:32.230
Then turn a little and throw a punch!

08:32.230 --> 08:34.240
Th-Throw a punch.

08:34.590 --> 08:37.240
Then put your hands up
 and shake, shake, shake.

08:37.240 --> 08:39.950
{bg}One, two, three, four!

08:39.950 --> 08:42.500
{bg}One, two, three, four...

08:42.880 --> 08:45.250
{bg}One, two, three, four!

08:45.250 --> 08:49.750
Right, left... Shake, shake, shake!

08:49.750 --> 08:52.260
<i>Why are they practicing when 
they're on different teams?</i>

08:52.570 --> 08:55.250
<i>I'd rather not do the cheer.</i>

08:56.990 --> 08:59.180
You've got this, Kono-san!

08:59.180 --> 09:00.620
D-Do I?

09:04.260 --> 09:06.200
Well, as long as they're having fun.

09:10.150 --> 09:13.150
<i>I like Sengoku-kun and Remi.</i>

09:13.870 --> 09:15.140
<i>I really do.</i>

09:16.290 --> 09:18.030
All you had to do was mix.

09:18.540 --> 09:20.400
You're angry.

09:20.990 --> 09:24.910
Whether I'm angry or not 
isn't the point right now.

09:24.910 --> 09:26.660
Should I add this?

09:24.910 --> 09:31.160
<b>Potato Starch</b>

09:26.660 --> 09:28.850
Hold it, Remi! That's not right!

09:28.850 --> 09:30.410
Read the label!

09:31.160 --> 09:33.420
That's the wrong thing. You need this, Remi.

09:31.160 --> 09:38.050
<b>Worcestershire</b>

09:33.420 --> 09:35.640
No! Sengoku-kun, stop!

09:35.640 --> 09:38.050
You don't add that now! 
Did you read the recipe?

09:40.610 --> 09:42.300
Watch what you're doing!

09:42.930 --> 09:46.760
Sakura, this says "salt." Is it salt?

09:42.930 --> 09:49.430
<b>Cooking Salt</b>

09:44.180 --> 09:49.430
<b>Salt</b>

09:46.760 --> 09:49.430
If it says salt, then it usually is!

09:49.940 --> 09:53.560
You're making too big a mess 
when you mix things!

09:54.170 --> 09:56.970
Sengoku-kun's group is 
still mixing ingredients.

09:56.970 --> 09:58.940
Class is nearly over.

09:59.450 --> 10:02.070
Never mind. Sengoku-kun, chop the vegetables.

10:02.070 --> 10:03.570
You can handle that, right?

10:03.980 --> 10:06.700
Huh? Chop? <i>Me</i>?

10:08.610 --> 10:09.790
Peel it first!

10:09.790 --> 10:11.670
Oops, I forgot.

10:11.670 --> 10:14.440
How can you not see the skin is still on?

10:15.010 --> 10:16.210
What about Remi?

10:17.110 --> 10:18.460
That's not how you hold it!

10:19.010 --> 10:21.250
No more knives for you!

10:21.250 --> 10:23.740
But I want to chop vegetables.

10:23.740 --> 10:25.750
Not right now.

10:25.750 --> 10:28.470
That's already going to give me nightmares.

10:29.080 --> 10:32.720
Just stir this slowly and carefully.

10:32.720 --> 10:34.820
And don't do anything else.

10:34.820 --> 10:37.020
Just stir it? Okay!

10:37.020 --> 10:37.480
<b><i>Ow</i></b>

10:37.020 --> 10:37.890
Ow.

10:38.360 --> 10:40.160
I cut myself.

10:41.550 --> 10:42.860
I need a bandage...

10:43.610 --> 10:46.060
Wait. You need to wash it first, Sengoku-kun.

10:46.060 --> 10:47.500
Oh, right.

10:48.120 --> 10:51.240
Now let's go get you a bandage.

10:52.020 --> 10:55.180
Sakura, is this stirred enough?

10:55.180 --> 10:56.880
Hey, Sakura?

10:57.250 --> 10:59.090
I'll put some of that stuff in.

10:59.090 --> 11:00.160
Huh?

11:00.160 --> 11:02.880
Hey, it's getting all wibbly.

11:03.430 --> 11:05.130
Are you done yet?

11:05.130 --> 11:07.560
Sakura, does this look right?

11:07.560 --> 11:09.360
Why is it smoking?!

11:10.040 --> 11:11.850
W-We need ventilation!

11:11.850 --> 11:14.080
What is this? It's getting in my eyes!

11:14.470 --> 11:16.510
Open the windows!

11:19.020 --> 11:24.350
<i>That's... how our last cooking class went.</i>

11:27.380 --> 11:29.180
Look at me.

11:29.180 --> 11:31.050
You're angry.

11:31.050 --> 11:33.130
Look at me so you understand!

11:33.130 --> 11:35.030
What are we making today?

11:35.430 --> 11:36.540
Curry.

11:36.540 --> 11:37.720
That's right.

11:38.180 --> 11:40.050
What ingredients did you bring?

11:40.050 --> 11:41.070
A daikon.

11:40.050 --> 11:42.050
<b>Daikon Radish</b>

11:41.070 --> 11:42.050
Why?!

11:42.050 --> 11:43.060
Tofu.

11:42.050 --> 11:44.050
<b>Tofu</b>

11:43.060 --> 11:44.050
Why?!

11:44.570 --> 11:47.910
Sengoku-kun, when you have curry at 
home, is there daikon in it?

11:47.910 --> 11:50.810
No, I don't think so.

11:51.140 --> 11:52.660
Then why did you bring one?

11:52.660 --> 11:56.710
I've only seen curry once 
it's already in a pot.

11:56.710 --> 11:59.940
I wasn't sure what to start with.

11:59.940 --> 12:03.150
With the vegetables you usually see in curry.

12:03.150 --> 12:03.950
Ah!

12:03.950 --> 12:07.930
Does placing vegetables around 
the pot bring forth the curry?

12:07.930 --> 12:09.330
You <i>cook</i> them!

12:09.850 --> 12:14.300
The class picked curry so that 
you two would be able to do this.

12:14.300 --> 12:16.710
Okay, tell me what you <i>can</i> make.

12:16.710 --> 12:18.150
Pasta.

12:18.150 --> 12:19.210
Croquettes.

12:19.210 --> 12:24.280
Warming up prepackaged food
does not count as "making" it.

12:24.280 --> 12:26.220
I-I know!

12:26.630 --> 12:30.100
Let's start by chipping 
the vegetables I brought—

12:30.100 --> 12:32.630
Ah! No knives for you, Remi!

12:34.350 --> 12:37.460
And you be careful, Sengoku-kun.

12:39.980 --> 12:42.610
<i>H-He's gotten better!</i>

12:42.960 --> 12:46.040
Wow, Sengoku-kun, you're doing great!

12:46.040 --> 12:48.700
That's it. Just peel off the skin—

12:49.120 --> 12:53.500
<b>The missing potato...</b>

12:49.930 --> 12:51.770
The potato disappeared!

12:51.770 --> 12:53.500
Why did you pare away the whole thing?

12:53.500 --> 12:58.250
<b>The missing onion...</b>

12:54.420 --> 12:56.150
The onion disappeared, too!

12:56.150 --> 12:58.250
You're not supposed to peel it to nothing!

12:58.250 --> 13:02.010
Well, the class thought this might happen

13:02.010 --> 13:05.410
and each group shared some of their 
curry with us. Isn't that great?

13:05.410 --> 13:07.000
<i>They know us too well.</i>

13:07.000 --> 13:09.100
Sengoku-kun, warm up the curry.

13:09.100 --> 13:11.020
Remi, plate the rice.

13:11.860 --> 13:15.020
Will I never be able to cook?

13:15.540 --> 13:18.520
If you work hard, 
I'm sure you will someday.

13:18.520 --> 13:20.930
The stove! Why are the flames so high?

13:21.970 --> 13:23.200
It was on high heat?

13:23.200 --> 13:25.310
High heat? <i>That</i> was high heat?

13:25.720 --> 13:27.760
What did you do?

13:27.760 --> 13:29.650
Sakura...

13:30.830 --> 13:34.790
I'm... I'm s... I'm s-s-sorry...

13:35.240 --> 13:38.460
The rice I made turned into gruel...

13:38.460 --> 13:40.020
Don't cry.

13:40.020 --> 13:41.460
Let it go.

13:42.000 --> 13:44.450
Rice gruel will work fine, right?

13:44.450 --> 13:46.090
Y-Yeah.

13:46.090 --> 13:50.100
Soupy rice gruel and gooey curry...

13:50.100 --> 13:51.690
L-Let's eat.

13:53.050 --> 13:54.720
Hey, it's pretty good.

13:54.720 --> 13:56.360
It's good, Remi.

13:56.360 --> 13:59.730
Yeah, but the rice isn't cooked all the way...

14:00.090 --> 14:01.640
Thank you guys, too.

14:01.640 --> 14:03.480
Nah, don't worry about it.

14:03.480 --> 14:05.950
I hope things turn out better next time.

14:06.440 --> 14:08.490
Sakura, I'm sorry.

14:08.490 --> 14:10.550
I mess everything up.

14:10.550 --> 14:14.240
It's okay. Everyone has things 
they're not good at.

14:14.870 --> 14:17.500
You'll make a great wife, Sakura.

14:17.500 --> 14:21.380
Huh? That takes much more than just cooking.

14:21.380 --> 14:24.220
But it's still better if you can cook.

14:24.630 --> 14:26.310
What should I do?

14:26.310 --> 14:28.550
No one will want to marry me.

14:28.550 --> 14:29.760
Me either.

14:29.760 --> 14:32.260
No one will want me.

14:33.260 --> 14:34.940
You'll be fine.

14:34.940 --> 14:39.340
If no one wants you, I'll marry you both.

14:42.910 --> 14:46.360
Thank you, Sakura! You're so cool!

14:46.360 --> 14:48.640
<i>Kono-san is boyfriend material.</i>

14:49.400 --> 14:52.280
Ta-da! Sports day T-shirts!

14:52.930 --> 14:54.350
The west shirts are over there.

14:54.350 --> 14:55.790
This is a medium size.

14:56.180 --> 14:57.980
Need a medium, Miyamura?

14:57.980 --> 14:59.610
Huh? A large.

14:59.610 --> 15:00.460
Maybe a small?

15:00.460 --> 15:02.290
Those are for girls.

15:02.290 --> 15:04.640
No mercy for the west team!

15:04.640 --> 15:06.050
Jeez, Miyamura.

15:07.530 --> 15:09.800
You're such a pushover.

15:09.800 --> 15:12.790
<i>Absolutely no slacking. Or else!</i>

15:14.990 --> 15:17.730
Then you're a pushover-over, Yoshikawa-san.

15:17.730 --> 15:19.310
That's too many overs!

15:19.670 --> 15:21.100
Hey, Yoshikawa.

15:21.100 --> 15:22.860
Got an extra west shirt in large?

15:22.860 --> 15:24.160
Sure do.

15:24.160 --> 15:27.410
You're on the committee, Toru,
so give me a hand.

15:27.410 --> 15:30.760
Yoshikawa-san,
do you have a small east shirt?

15:30.760 --> 15:33.180
Yoshikawa, where are the west mediums?

15:33.180 --> 15:35.250
Yuki-chan, do you have a west small?

15:35.850 --> 15:37.470
For crying out loud...

15:37.470 --> 15:40.080
Just get them yourselves!

15:40.080 --> 15:41.850
Whoa!

15:42.510 --> 15:45.960
By the way, what'd you enter, Miyamura?

15:45.960 --> 15:49.210
Hmm... The 100-meter, I think.

15:49.210 --> 15:51.250
You should be in the relay.

15:51.990 --> 15:53.730
No, that's too much pressure!

15:53.730 --> 15:55.990
That's just for the track team.

15:55.990 --> 15:59.980
Not really. Shu did it as a first-year.

15:59.980 --> 16:04.480
<b>Track Team</b>

16:01.280 --> 16:03.040
Though the track team did smoke him.

16:03.040 --> 16:04.480
Uh...

16:04.480 --> 16:07.890
Well, the other team has the president.

16:07.890 --> 16:11.990
Yeah, that really improves 
our chances of winning.

16:12.310 --> 16:15.170
I hope he comes to sports day.

16:15.170 --> 16:17.280
He should at least come to school.

16:17.280 --> 16:18.410
This is our last sports day.

16:18.410 --> 16:20.250
<b>The president may
cease to exist that day</b>

16:18.850 --> 16:20.250
Rain!

16:20.250 --> 16:24.690
All of the boys have to do the mock 
cavalry battle and topple-the-pole.

16:24.690 --> 16:27.580
The other events are coed.

16:28.030 --> 16:30.380
Cheer practice looks pretty hard.

16:30.380 --> 16:33.270
<i>Hori-san will be cheering too, right?</i>

16:33.270 --> 16:34.880
You look great, Hori-san!

16:34.880 --> 16:36.730
So cool!

16:36.730 --> 16:37.840
Really?

16:37.840 --> 16:39.640
That decides it!

16:40.050 --> 16:41.950
How do you think I look, Miyamura?

16:41.950 --> 16:43.020
It's complicated.

16:43.020 --> 16:44.020
Huh?

16:44.450 --> 16:46.660
<i>It's not what I pictured.</i>

16:47.730 --> 16:53.220
And in this sentence,
this noun gets modified...

16:53.220 --> 16:55.380
so make sure not to get confused.

16:56.620 --> 16:57.460
<b>Monstrous
Rage</b>

17:00.470 --> 17:02.900
<i>Wh-What gives, Hori?</i>

17:00.620 --> 17:04.130
<b>Deathly Chill</b>

17:06.500 --> 17:09.510
<b>Haunting Aura</b>

17:08.090 --> 17:09.510
<i>Ghostly rapping!</i>

17:10.380 --> 17:13.340
Now read the next sentence, Hori.

17:15.330 --> 17:17.270
"It's mine."

17:17.600 --> 17:20.350
You can ease up on the emotion a bit.

17:20.350 --> 17:21.520
How would you translate that?

17:21.520 --> 17:23.840
Get away from her, idiot.

17:24.330 --> 17:26.240
Where does it say that?

17:29.290 --> 17:32.280
She just forgot her textbook.

17:32.740 --> 17:35.040
Yeah? That so?

17:35.430 --> 17:36.560
Yes!

17:36.560 --> 17:38.030
I was just showing her mine.

17:39.610 --> 17:40.530
Hey!

17:44.070 --> 17:44.850
Oh no!

17:44.850 --> 17:46.420
"Oh no" what?!

17:46.770 --> 17:49.280
You're angry at me, Hori-san.

17:49.280 --> 17:52.400
Y-You don't need to be scared. 
I haven't said anything.

17:52.880 --> 17:56.930
I have nothing to hide. I swear.

17:56.930 --> 18:00.890
But... I wasn't worried about that!

18:00.890 --> 18:01.970
I just...

18:03.710 --> 18:04.940
Never mind.

18:09.860 --> 18:12.450
You're scary when you get jealous, Hori.

18:12.450 --> 18:14.230
Jealous?

18:14.230 --> 18:16.190
I wasn't feeling jealous.

18:16.630 --> 18:18.180
It was more like murderous.

18:19.050 --> 18:22.710
Maybe you should stick 
to jealousy from now on.

18:23.020 --> 18:24.270
Was it just you?

18:25.010 --> 18:27.780
Were you the only one feeling jealous?

18:27.780 --> 18:29.430
Oh, well...

18:32.090 --> 18:37.850
Things I can say to reassure her

18:32.640 --> 18:37.850
<b>Maybe he just 
doesn't show it.</b>

18:33.140 --> 18:37.850
<b>I'm sure he's 
jealous deep down.</b>

18:33.640 --> 18:37.850
<b>You're <i>too</i>
 jealous, Hori!</b>

18:34.140 --> 18:35.560
<b>Don't sweat it!</b>

18:34.640 --> 18:37.850
<b>All guys are
 like that!</b>

18:35.560 --> 18:37.850
<b>Don't sweat it!</b>

18:38.210 --> 18:39.410
Don't sweat it!

18:39.920 --> 18:41.090
Thanks...

18:43.590 --> 18:45.700
Hey, it's Hori-san.

18:45.700 --> 18:46.850
Miyamura?

18:46.850 --> 18:48.320
And Toru!

18:48.320 --> 18:49.860
You've even got Yoshikawa.

18:49.860 --> 18:51.470
You almost done painting?

18:51.470 --> 18:52.860
Just about.

18:53.540 --> 18:57.910
They called a meeting for the sports day 
committee third-years over the intercom.

18:57.910 --> 19:00.360
They said to come as soon as you can.

19:00.360 --> 19:03.190
What? But I'm not quite finished.

19:03.190 --> 19:04.770
I can wrap up the painting.

19:04.770 --> 19:05.870
Thanks—

19:06.470 --> 19:08.980
Hori, what was your grade in art class?

19:08.980 --> 19:10.280
Why bring that up?

19:10.280 --> 19:12.130
Just get going already.

19:13.880 --> 19:17.310
Thanks! I'll be back right after the meeting.

19:19.770 --> 19:21.940
I just need to paint inside the lines, right?

19:21.940 --> 19:23.640
Easy enough.

19:24.140 --> 19:26.640
Yuki was worried for nothing.

19:30.250 --> 19:32.810
I wish I had worn my blazer.

19:32.810 --> 19:35.770
Hori, aren't you cold out here?

19:36.270 --> 19:37.780
Mizouchi.

19:37.780 --> 19:39.360
Yeah, I'm cold.

19:39.770 --> 19:42.140
Girls have to put up with bare legs.

19:46.760 --> 19:48.150
Keep that over your lap.

19:48.150 --> 19:49.410
It won't be as bad.

19:50.180 --> 19:51.920
You can return it when you're done.

19:51.920 --> 19:53.860
Wait, Mizouchi!

19:54.990 --> 19:57.100
I might get paint on it.

20:01.190 --> 20:02.300
Hori-san!

20:03.610 --> 20:04.610
You done?

20:04.610 --> 20:06.730
You startled me.

20:06.730 --> 20:08.680
I'm not done yet.

20:12.190 --> 20:13.370
Whose is that?

20:13.940 --> 20:15.360
Mizouchi's.

20:15.830 --> 20:18.720
I said my legs were cold,

20:18.720 --> 20:19.940
and he let me borrow it.

20:40.720 --> 20:42.420
This is warmer than a blazer.

20:43.250 --> 20:46.690
Because I've been wearing it.

20:48.640 --> 20:49.700
Thanks.

20:53.200 --> 20:54.200
You're gonna wear it?!

20:54.200 --> 20:55.640
He'll never know.

20:55.640 --> 20:57.140
Maybe, but...

20:57.940 --> 20:59.920
Want to help me, Miyamura?

21:01.110 --> 21:03.490
It's my first time using paint like this.

21:05.160 --> 21:06.860
Wait, isn't that...

21:10.740 --> 21:12.620
<b>Destroying
the evidence</b>

21:20.370 --> 21:21.370
Hori.

21:22.440 --> 21:23.630
You done?

21:23.630 --> 21:25.530
Oh, yeah.

21:25.530 --> 21:26.630
Thanks.

21:27.110 --> 21:28.520
Not cold anymore?

21:28.520 --> 21:29.540
Nope.

21:30.470 --> 21:33.140
Let me know if you need anything.

21:36.330 --> 21:39.270
I hope Mizouchi-kun just keeps walking

21:39.270 --> 21:45.420
and will never know the difference
between your body heat and mine.

21:45.770 --> 21:47.680
Honestly...

21:49.650 --> 21:51.160
Are you jealous?

21:52.120 --> 21:53.160
You are!

22:01.140 --> 22:03.460
What are you giggling about?

22:04.710 --> 22:09.460
She had it on her lap,
 but the sleeves are warm?

23:36.560 --> 23:40.020
Next time
page.3 Sports Day
